s in my custom build of 4.3, custom because precision=double, otherwise it's the 4.3 branch)\n\n\n\n\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Ubuntu 24.04.2 LTS 24.04 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3090 (nvidia; 550.144.03) - AMD Ryzen 9 9900X 12-Core Processor (24 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI'm writing a custom 3D editor, and I need a separate window to edit a specific data type, and this window must be able to be maximized on a second monitor, so I need a native window.  The use case is I want the user to be able to manipulate items in the main window, and have the changes appear in a secondary window which is full screen on another monitor (which is projected via projector onto a flat surface). \n\nWhen I open that secondary window, any OptionButton popups have their popup appear in the original main window. \n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/28bd7fa0-26f1-411e-914b-8409d594a83e)\n\nIn the screenshot the popup menu with the options should appear in the secondary window appropriately placed below the OptionButton, they incorrectly appear in the main window. \n\nI have not tested menus, or other UI controls which popup additional views. \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Download and open the MRP\n2. Click the play button\n3. Then click the 'Open Secondary Window' button in the main view\n4. Then click the OptionButton in the secondary window\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[menubug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20431875/menubug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_use